\begin{problem}[The fixed point property for reflexive Banach spaces]
Let $X$ be a reflexive Banach space, $C \subseteq X$ nonempty, closed, bounded and convex, and $T : C \to C$ nonexpansive, i.e. $\left\| T x - T y \right\| \le \left\| x - y \right\|$ for all $x, y \in C$. Must $T$ have a fixed point?
\end{problem}

\end{document}
